  "title": "Departments – Town of Hancock",
  "text": "Departments – Town of Hancock\nTown of Hancock\nDepartments\nCalendar\nForms\nContact\nPoints of Interest\nAttractions / Misc.\nCamping\nFood\nLodging\nPhotos\nPayments\nDepartments\nAssessors\nBoard of Health\nCommittees\nCouncil on Aging\nEducation\nFire Department\nHighway / Roads\nInspectors\nLibrary\nPolice Department\nTax Collector\nTown Clerk\nTransfer Station\nHancock is a quiet, peaceful town about twenty miles long and three miles wide, bordered on the east by the famous Berkshire hills, and on the west by the rugged Taconic range.\nHancock is the longest and narrowest town in Berkshire County.  The northern portion of the town is separated from the southern portion by a mountain.  One has to drive through a couple of towns to the east or drive west into New York to get from one end to the other.\n413-738-5225\n3650 Hancock Road\nPO Box 1084, Hancock, MA 01237\nThe Town Hall is open every week day (except holidays) between 9:00 AM and 12:00 noon.",
